# Go Quality

- Target the Go version declared in `go.mod`.
- Keep packages cohesive and dependencies minimal.
- Accept interfaces at boundaries; return concrete types by default.
- Wrap errors with context and expose typed errors when callers branch on them.
- Pass `context.Context` first for future cancellable I/O.
- Avoid package globals except immutable constants.
- Keep canonical DTOs free of maps and nondeterministic metadata.
- Initialize JSON slices through constructors or normalization.
- Write table-driven tests when multiple contract cases share behavior.
- Run `gofmt`, `go test ./...`, and `go vet ./...`.
